# weapons.rec: the weapons, every one of them a record here and nowhere else (rogue/kinds.go
# reads it); a new record is a new weapon. mktiles.py cuts the pictures onto tiles16.png
# and fills in the icons, the remapper (remap_weapons.sh) re-maps them; every other field
# is yours. icon: cell of tiles16.png; -1: unassigned. picture: the source picture (an
# animation strip's first 16px frame). Dice are Rogue's.
#
#   kind      melee, launcher or projectile
#   hands     1 or 2
#   edge      sharp (thrown or shot, it sticks) or blunt (it bounces and drops)
#   reach     melee: blocks, plus the target's size      swing: ticks between blows
#   damage    dice wielded                                thrown: dice thrown, or shot from its launcher
#   missile   yes: flies well thrown (Rogue's ISMISSL)
#   launcher  a projectile's launcher (one line each)
#   action    a launcher's: bow (held to draw), crossbow (spanned with R), sling (whirled)
#   speed     a launcher's blocks per tick at full power; draw: a bow's ticks to a full draw;
#             charge: a crossbow's ticks to span a chamber; magazine: its chambers; cooldown: ticks between shots
#   fly       how it flies thrown or shot: tumble (end over end, the default), spear (tip first, rolling),
#             tip (its mesh, the tip at the point), cube (its mesh, resting flat)
#   mesh      a glb file (assets/meshes, tools/mkmeshes made them): a projectile's model, the sling's rest and whirl
#   sweeps    yes: the sideways swing strikes every monster in its arc
#   backstab  the damage multiplier on a sleeping monster (2 without)
#   worth     what the fighters guild pays
#   sound     the sound event of a blow or a shot (assets/sounds/sounds.json)
#   attack    a melee attack: a Better Combat animation (assets/bettercombat) and the fraction of it where the blow
#             lands, one line each in the order of the attack patterns (sideways swing, overhead strike, stab:
#             left button, right button, F); horizontal slashes alternate as a combo
#   hand      first-person display: rotation, translation, scale (item/handheld without); hand3: third person's

%rec: Tileset
id: tiles16
name: VoxelRogue 16px tiles
file: tiles16.png
tile_w: 16
tile_h: 16
off_x: 0
off_y: 0
gap_x: 0
gap_y: 0

